        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Does is the third-person singular present form of the verb \"do\", pronounced /d\u028cz/."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Usage as a Verb"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Third-Person Singular: Use \"does\" with subjects like he, she, it, or singular nouns (the dog, my friend) in the present tense.",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Example: \"She does her homework after school.\""
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Auxiliary (Helping) Verb: Use it to form questions and negative sentences.",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Question Example: \"Does he like music?\""
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Negative Example: \"It does not make sense.\""
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Other Meanings"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Plural Noun: \"Does\" is the plural form of doe (a female deer, rabbit, or antelope).",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Example: \"We saw three does in the woods.\""
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
